      "1": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "ADD\nThe add node adds all incoming values up and outputs the sum.\n\nThe following patch contains all the basic math functions in Wire.\nThe radius of the red ring is directly modulated by the Add node.\n\nPatch Explained -\n\n• The Sine provides a signal running from 0.1 to 0.6.\n• The basic math functions adjust this signal before running it to the Join node.\n• Join puts all inputs into an array so that each channel can modulate one instance of the circle.\n"
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
